Question 1 - Kimberley asks Since suicide

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.579
squad will be more prominent on the show are
we to expect the appearance of Harley Quinn?

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:46.579
﻿

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.700
After her cameo this season Andrew Kriesberg
said that they never had any intention of

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.410
making her a real character on the show. It
was just meant to be an Easter egg for the

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:57.121
hardcore fans. But never say never. Stephen
Amell said this funny thing recently. Someone

00:00:57.121 --> 00:01:02.640
asked him about Diggle becoming the John Stewart
Green Lantern and he invoked hollywoodntv

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.880
rules. He joked that in the world of TV, if
it looks good, it has a much better chance

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.880
of happening.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.310
I think that Cassidy Alexa looked really good,
so there's a good chance we could see her

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:17.679
again. But I don't think it will be a big
huge role like the other Suicide Squad members.

00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:21.931
Question 2 - Aramil Whisperwind asks how will
the timeline’s work with Oliver and Barry

00:01:21.931 --> 00:01:24.950
going on each other’s shows without missing
their own episodes?

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.929
So you're asking how can Oliver be in Central
City doing Flash stuff at the same time he's

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:32.889
supposed to be on screen in Starling. What
they'd probably do in a situation like that

00:01:32.889 --> 00:01:37.990
is write around the problem. So events are
separated by days. Like Oliver goes to Central

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.859
City on a Tuesday but is back in the New Arrowcave
by Wednesday.

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:45.689
And right now we have no idea what the crossovers
are going to look like except for what we

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:50.389
saw in the trailer. And that was Barry visiting
Oliver in The first episode of the Flash.

00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:54.420
Because both shows are premiering the same
week. Arrow episode 1 will probably just pick

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:59.070
up that next day unless Grant Gustin comes
on Arrow. Which is totally possible.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.920
It sounds confusing but it's really not. Whenever
episodes start again I'll try to address the

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.869
timelines of both shows throughout the season.

00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:10.560
Question 3 - Sventu asks which other Justice
League members do you think we’ll see next

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.560
